sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch08-01> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "For systems with complex behavior, a model cannot be adequately assessed by matching a few extracted numbers; the best first test is a visual comparison of the model's overall behavior with that of the real system.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Models of complex systems should first be judged by comparing overall pictures";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 8, “Implications for Everyday Systems”; section “Issues of Modelling” (from p. 363), p. 365. Scope: scientific modelling of systems with complex behavior"
}
